<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea buys 544,500 T of grain, oilseeds in Feb.</title>
<headline>S.Korea buys 544,500 T of grain, oilseeds in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea bought at least 544,500 tonnes of grains and oilseeds during February through tenders and private negotiations, traders said.</p>
<p>The total broke down into 216,500 tonnes of corn, 36,400 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 85,000 tonnes of feed wheat, 135,000 tonnes of U.S. soybean, 10,000 tonnes of Chinese cottonseed meal, 26,100 tonnes of Indian rapeseed meal, 12,500 tonnes of Chinese wheatbran pellet, 10,000 tonnes of palm kernel meal and 13,000 tonnes of copra.</p>
<p>This compared with a total of 1,076,800 tonnes purchased in January.  </p>
